From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Novikov <dj.novikov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0500
Subject: net: phy: micrel: ksz9477: keep the PHY powered on suspend

"ip link set lanX down" halts the PHY, and phylib suspends it:
genphy_suspend() sets BMCR_PDOWN. On "ip link set lanX up"
ksz9477_resume() clears it, and as its own comment says, leaving
power-down generates an internal global reset. On KSZ9567 that reset
can take down the link of other ports of the switch.

Seen on NAPI-Switch (KSZ9567) in an MRP ring with 1000BASE-T links on
lan2, lan3, lan5 and lan1 at 100 Mbit: in 2 of 3 cases bringing one
port up dropped the links of other ports for about 3 s. Once both ring
ports went down together, so the ring was cut for 2.8 s although only
one link had been toggled. A cable pulled or plugged at the far end
never did this: the PHY is not powered down then.

Do not power the PHY down on suspend. Take the link down instead:
advertise nothing and restart autonegotiation, the link partner loses
the link as with a pulled cable. phy_start() puts the advertisement
back through config_aneg. ksz9477_resume() finds BMCR_PDOWN clear and
does nothing, so no global reset. Unused ports, which ksz9477.c powers
down at setup, are not affected.

The cost is the power of an idle PHY on an administratively down port.
---
 drivers/net/phy/micrel.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/micrel.c b/drivers/net/phy/micrel.c
--- a/drivers/net/phy/micrel.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/micrel.c
@@ -2487,6 +2487,31 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* Powering a KSZ9477 PHY up again generates an internal global reset (see
+ * ksz9477_resume()), and that reset can drop the link of the other PHYs of
+ * the switch: on a ring both ring ports go down when one port is brought up
+ * with "ip link set up". So a suspend leaves the PHY powered and only takes
+ * the link down: advertise nothing and restart autonegotiation, the link
+ * partner sees the link go away as with a pulled cable. phy_start() writes
+ * the advertisement back through config_aneg.
+ */
+static int ksz9477_suspend(struct phy_device *phydev)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = phy_modify(phydev, MII_ADVERTISE,
+			 ADVERTISE_ALL | ADVERTISE_PAUSE_CAP | ADVERTISE_PAUSE_ASYM, 0);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = phy_modify(phydev, MII_CTRL1000,
+			 ADVERTISE_1000FULL | ADVERTISE_1000HALF, 0);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	return genphy_restart_aneg(phydev);
+}
+
 static int ksz8061_resume(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	int ret;
@@ -6629,7 +6654,7 @@
 	.config_aneg	= ksz9477_config_aneg,
 	.read_status	= ksz9477_read_status,
 	.handle_interrupt = kszphy_handle_interrupt,
-	.suspend	= genphy_suspend,
+	.suspend	= ksz9477_suspend,
 	.resume		= ksz9477_resume,
 	.get_phy_stats	= kszphy_get_phy_stats,
 	.update_stats	= kszphy_update_stats,
